WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.060
Eat a meal rich in protein, and you
take in more amino acids than you need.

2
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.330
But surplus amino acids cannot be stored.

3
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.880
Their amino groups become ammonia.

4
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.470
Ammonia is highly toxic, and very soluble.

5
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.720
And about three-quarters of your liver's
blood arrives straight from the gut.

6
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:22.700
So if your body makes enough
ammonia to poison itself every day,

7
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.220
why doesn't it?

8
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.820
In this mission, you'll
trace blood into the liver,

9
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.110
through its four main vessels.

10
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.310
Then you'll zoom into a lobule,
a tiny hexagon of liver cells,

11
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.900
and draw what you see
under the microscope.

12
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:41.170
Your mission: find out why the ammonia
you make every day doesn't poison you.
